nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb35c7712ffe4EY95ILbHqsaQK type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +2ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +1ms service=session session=ses_eb35c7712ffe4EY95ILbHqsaQK sessionID=ses_eb35c7712ffe4EY95ILbHqsaQK unlocking\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/`, but I haven't run `python3 -m unittest` because I don't have a way to run commands here. I checked each change against the tests by reading them, and I think the whole suite should pass now. Please run it to confirm.\n\n- **`fees.py`**: the late fee added the daily rate instead of multiplying by it. Changed `days_late + DAILY_FEE` to `days_late * DAILY_FEE`, so 4 days late is now 1.00.\n- **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the policy comment and the tests both say members can hold 5 books. Set it to 5.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n` events, and an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n- **`factory.py`**: the sample data was missing the third book. Added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`.\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` kept the year as text, so `age()` couldn't subtract it. It now converts the year with `int(year)`.\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from `catalog.nonexistent`, a module that doesn't exist. Now it imports from `catalog.text`.INFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=app name=lsp shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=app name=session shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:32:53 +0ms service=app name=mcp shutdown\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "par